Z||000004||BAM-BAM||09-26-2000||11:03 AM||||  Thanks guys, I am going to take some before and after pics to show the contrast. Mike said it would be about three weeks to get the goods, but at this point I'll be patient. In the mean time, I am going to the wreckers and getting a solid charcoal dash and the dark grey interior pieces. I just won an E-Bay bid for new door glass. I E-Mailed the seller first and was reassured that the glass was clear and free of scratches. I am getting a new windshield installed this week sometime. The next real expensive piece is going to be the center auto shift console. I found them new for $225.00, I really don't want to pay that much, but for the continuity and appearence that I am looking for, I just may have to. We'll see. Aside from the stereo components(which may have to wait) that should complete my interior. I'm a little behind schedule but that's ok. After the interior is finished I am going to work on the exterior panels and trim. I hope to go to paint summer of next year. Of course that all depends on what I get done with the engine after the first of the year. There deffinitely will be a swap of some kind just not sure what yet. Anyway, Thanks again and keep your eyes peeled. Pics will be coming in the near future.<P> Late, BAM OUT!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
